What are you doing reading an unknown scroll while wearing valuable armor???
If I haven't already found a destroy armor scroll, I take off any valuable
armor before I read an unknown scroll.

If I haven't already found a scroll of fire or a scroll of identify, there is
a real conflict between holding all unidentified burnables so I can identify
them just in case it's a scroll of identify, or drop them just in case it's a
scroll of fire.

Learn how to use the good points of heavy balls.  Learn the many ways to get
rid of them.  Be aware of the consequences of reading ANY unknown scroll.
Before you read an unknown scroll, check which scroll types are still
unfound and be prepared for the consequences of any of them.  Take preventive
action before reading it if appropriate.  I often carry un-ID'd stuff around
until I'm prepared to handle any bad results.  Learn the relative frequencies
of scrolls.  If you have five of one type of scroll, it's probably not either
genocide or punishment...

Learn how to prevent erasure of scrollbooks in case you accidentally step
into a pool.

There are ways to get around all problems.  That's part of the game.  I get
in a hurry sometimes and lose valuable armor.  That's part of the game.  I've
has scrolls erased by stepping in a pool.  I've learned from that.  I've made
many mistakes, and learned from them.

In some much earlier incarnations of hack, restoring from backups wasn't even
possible.  The time stamp of the file and ITS PHYSICAL LOCATION ON THE DISK
were stored in the save file!  Making a backup and restoring it just didn't
work!  I was very disappointed when I discovered that that was no longer the
case in nethack.

